MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The smart plug and Alexa-compatible cameras give my existing Echo devices useful new jobs, which makes them feel like natural additions.",
    "The powered USB hub fits my repeated use of keyboards, mice, adapters and other computer peripherals by offering more connections and individual switches."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The older Echo Dot and Fire TV Sticks repeat functions covered by my newer Echo Dot, Echo Show and Fire TV Stick 4K Max; sharing the same product family does not give me a reason to buy them.",
    "The card-reader bundle duplicates equipment I already have, while the smaller memory cards and USB-C cables do not address a current need. The 256GB card interests me, but I would need to identify a compatible device that needs the extra storage."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My recent Alexa purchases seem to have been taken as interest in any Echo or Fire TV device, even an older version of something I already own.",
    "My history with storage and computer accessories seems to have been taken as an ongoing need for more cards, readers and cables, regardless of what they would add."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My recent purchases establish what I already have: useful additions appeal more than replacements that offer no clear improvement.",
    "An accessory needs a specific purpose and compatible equipment. More storage is only a possible purchase, while adding voice control or powered USB connections has a clearer use for me."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my Alexa setup and peripheral use, but sometimes confuse expanding what I can do with duplicating equipment I already own."
}
